# expect: expected an expression, found `+`
# The other half of accept/list_newline_separators.dawn's `leading_minus`. `+`
# and `-` are the two operators that may not lead a continuation line (spec
# §1.7), so inside a multi-line literal a line opening with one of them opens an
# *element*. `-` has a prefix meaning and gets it; `+` has none, so the element
# position it now stands in is where it is refused. The diagnostic moved here
# from `expected `]`` when newlines became separators, and it points at the same
# token either way.
fn f(a: Int, b: Int) -> List[Int] = [
  a
  + b
]
